# Not part of the site: internal instructions for whoever works on this
# surface. assets.directory is this dir, so without this line the file is
# served at the surface's public URL.
CLAUDE.md
cross/CLAUDE.md

# Neither are these. They are part of the repo, not the site: the deploy would
# otherwise upload a 1.7 MB word list nothing fetches (the committed
# lexicon.dawg is what the browser and the worker read), plus the test and
# build scripts. dict/lexicon.dawg is deliberately NOT here — offline play
# fetches it.
dict/enable1.txt
test/
tools/
cross/test/
cross/tools/

# The crossword's own artefacts, on the other hand, ARE the site:
# cross/dict/answers.txt is fetched by the generator in the browser, and
# cross/dict/clues/*.txt are read by the worker through the ASSETS binding —
# an asset the worker cannot fetch is a puzzle with no clues.
cross/dict/MANIFEST.json

# SERVER-ONLY CODE, and a real leak until this was added. `assets.directory` is
# this whole dir, so anything here that is not ignored is published — and that
# included the worker itself, plus the bundle and FULL SOURCE MAP wrangler
# writes into .wrangler/tmp while deploying. The temp directory is named
# randomly per deploy, so every deploy was leaving another copy of the server's
# source map in the asset manifest, permanently reachable:
#
#     https://words.mino.mobi/.wrangler/tmp/deploy-XXXXXX/worker.js.map   200
#
# Ignoring `worker.js` here does NOT unhook the worker: `main` in
# wrangler.jsonc is bundled separately, and .assetsignore only governs what is
# uploaded as a STATIC ASSET. Nothing in the browser fetches either path.
worker.js
lib/
.wrangler/
